    {
      "id": "antony-and-cleopatra/sceneIII_3.1/p@94170",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "VENTIDIUS.\nNow, darting Parthia, art thou struck, and now\nPleased Fortune does of Marcus Crassus’ death\nMake me revenger. Bear the king’s son’s body\nBefore our army. Thy Pacorus, Orodes,\nPays this for Marcus Crassus.",
